**Read:** [Oxide-scale growth and discontinuities — Ulrich, Glatzel and Galetz](../sources/Oxide-Scale-Kinetics-Ulrich-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_5ZVWBZKX1ATCMAF2H08XD87C6K) in full; the earlier thermal mismatch and interface-fracture Records.

Growth strain and thermal-expansion mismatch can load an oxide film and its interface. A mass trace can combine oxygen uptake, volatile products, detached scale and renewed exposure of substrate. Even a small net mass change can conceal considerable reaction. Collection of spalled material and cross-sectional evidence help close the account.

**Work:** Reconstruct a thermal cycle and estimate the mismatch strain under stated constraints, then explain why that estimate alone does not determine delamination. Compare an intact-scale kinetic model with one allowing measured loss or discontinuities. Use the primary article to test whether an inferred jump reflects a plausible local event, and distinguish fitted discontinuity parameters from independently observed crack or spallation geometry.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
